            <ArticleTitle>[A woman with 'strange bumps' on her feet].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>A2576</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 57-year-old woman came to the dermatologist because of 'strange bumps' on her feet. The bumps were not painful. On physical examination bumps were seen on the medial parts of her left foot, near the sole. They had the same colour as the skin and decreased in size while sitting. The diagnosis was: 'piezogenic papules'.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
